From 09e07bb0000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@avtonarx.local>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 08:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(parser): reject spare-parts/accessory listings
 mis-categorized as cars
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Even inside the correctly-scoped '/transport/legkovye-avtomobili/' OLX
category, some sellers list spare parts (engine, bumper, etc.) with the
model name in the title (e.g. 'Chevrolet Cobalt dvigatel sotiladi'),
which TitleModelMatcher accepts since the model name genuinely is there.

Added AccessoryListingDetector: a narrow, high-precision keyword list
(zapchast/na razbor/bufer ot/etc.) checked at parser extraction time,
right after the title-model match check. Rejected items are logged to
parser_rejection_logs (code: accessory_or_part_listing) for audit, same
pattern as the existing olx_fallback_result / title_model_mismatch checks.

Note: this only affects newly-scraped listings going forward — raw
titles are not persisted to market_listings (per TZ, no full description
storage), so this cannot be applied retroactively via
listings:cleanup-suspicious.
